<section class="day-guide-container page">
  <h1>A day at Desire</h1>
  <p>Whether you're feeling excited, curious, a little nervous, or all of the above, that's completely normal. Here's how a typical day tends to flow, so you can relax into it rather than guess your way through the first one.</p>
  <p>Desire has a <strong>playful, social, adults-only energy</strong>, but there's no single right way to do it. Join in, watch from the sidelines, keep things private, or mix and mingle as much as feels good. <strong>Comfort, consent, and personal boundaries</strong> are part of the culture everywhere on property.</p>
  <p class="small-text" style="color: var(--color-espresso-soft);">Times, dress codes, and reservation policies below reflect typical patterns and can change&mdash;confirm current details with the resort before your trip.</p>

  <div class="property-toggle">
    <button type="button" class="toggle-btn active" aria-pressed="true" data-target="drm">Desire Riviera Maya</button>
    <button type="button" class="toggle-btn" aria-pressed="false" data-target="pearl">Desire Pearl</button>
  </div>

  <div class="day-guide" data-property="drm">
    <h2>Morning: coffee, breakfast, and getting settled</h2>
    <p>Start with coffee at the bar near the gym, croissants and small sandwiches often on offer there too. For a fuller breakfast, head to the buffet, or ease into the morning with room service (an extra fee may apply). Most guests settle into the pool after, if you want a cabana or specific chairs, check with the pool staff, they'll tell you what's open. When the resort is full, good spots go quickly, worth checking back around 10:30am if nothing's free right away.</p>

    <h2>Late morning: planning the day</h2>
    <p>On the way to the activity pool, check the daily activity board, your cheat sheet for the day's games, the evening's theme, and the night's entertainment. This is also a good moment to think about dinner. Reservations for Eros are typically made around midday near the activity pool, and in true Desire fashion, plenty of dinners happen spontaneously too, a couple you've met might invite you to join them.</p>

    <h2>Lunch and afternoon</h2>
    <p>Keep it easy at the buffet near the Quiet Pool, order from the menu at Eros by the activity pool, or grab something from the grill nearby. From there, the day tends to settle into a few main spots.</p>

    <table class="vibe-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Location</th><th>Vibe</th><th>Useful for</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Quiet Pool</td><td>Relaxed, low-key</td><td>Calmer connection</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Jenny's Beach Bar</td><td>Caribbean views</td><td>Nicer drinks, conversation</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Activity Pool</td><td>Lively, social</td><td>Swim-up bar, volleyball, games</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <p>Nothing here is required. Watching, laughing, or floating with a drink in hand is just as much a part of the day as jumping in.</p>

    <h2>Late afternoon: hot tub time</h2>
    <p>Around 5pm, many guests head to the hot tub above the lobby (there's an elevator if you'd rather skip the stairs). It's a popular window for drinks and mingling, and a good indicator of where the evening's headed. Cubbies are available for your things, and a handful of cabana beds nearby, follow your own comfort level and communicate clearly as the vibe unfolds.</p>

    <h2>Evening: dinner and dress codes</h2>
    <table class="dining-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Restaurant</th><th>Cuisine</th><th>Reservations</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Buffet</td><td>Varied</td><td>Generally open, no reservation typically needed</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Jade</td><td>Asian-inspired</td><td>Reservation typically required</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Sahl&oacute;</td><td>Fine dining</td><td>Required, 1+ hour experience</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Eros</td><td>Mediterranean</td><td>Required, book around midday</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Kahlo</td><td>Mexican</td><td>Required</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Room service</td><td>Varied</td><td>Extra fee may apply</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <p>Gentlemen are generally expected to wear long pants and closed-toe shoes at restaurants other than the buffet, though dress codes can vary by venue and change over time.</p>

    <h2>Night: shows and the dance floor</h2>
    <p>Entertainment typically starts around 10pm near the lobby, with shows generally running an hour to ninety minutes, though schedules can change. Free tables are first-come, first-served. Afterward, most people head upstairs for dancing and the evening's theme. Later still, the crowd often drifts back to the hot tub from midnight on, sometimes running until 3am or later. Go at your own pace, and keep it respectful and clear for the people around you.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="day-guide" data-property="pearl" hidden>
    <h2>Morning: coffee, breakfast, and getting settled</h2>
    <p>Addiction, Pearl's coffee corner, is an easy first stop for espresso and something fresh-baked. For a fuller breakfast, Aphrodite's buffet has you covered, or order room service if you'd rather ease in slowly (an extra fee may apply). Once you're ready for the pool, check with staff about chairs or a cabana, spots fill up fastest when the resort is busy.</p>

    <h2>Late morning: planning the day</h2>
    <p>Look for the daily activity board on your way to the pool, it lists the day's games, the evening's theme, and the night's entertainment. Worth thinking about dinner around now too, Pearl's specialty restaurants are smaller in number than at Riviera Maya, so reserving earlier in the day is a good habit if there's somewhere specific you want to eat.</p>

    <h2>Lunch and afternoon</h2>
    <p>Aphrodite's buffet is the easy lunch option. Pearl's pool is one continuous space rather than two separate ones, the far end near the activity area stays noticeably quieter, so it's easy to find your spot whether you want the energy or a bit of distance from it. Lush does double duty as both the pool bar and beach bar, a relaxed, dependable option rather than a big scene of its own.</p>

    <table class="vibe-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Location</th><th>Vibe</th><th>Useful for</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
