    <p>Gentlemen are generally expected to wear long pants and closed-toe shoes at restaurants other than the buffet, though dress codes can vary by venue and change over time.</p>

    <h2>Night: shows and the dance floor</h2>
    <p>Nightly entertainment leads into dancing at Obsession, Pearl's nightclub. Free tables are first-come, first-served, and reservations generally aren't needed. Later on, the crowd tends to drift back toward The Wet Spot, sometimes running well past midnight. Go at your own pace, and keep it respectful and clear for the people around you.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>A few helpful tips, either resort</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Tipping isn't required, but can be appreciated, especially when staff provide extra help throughout your stay.</li>
    <li>The Premier membership presentation can be declined. It runs 1 to 2 hours, only worth it if you're genuinely interested.</li>
    <li>Quintana Roo's tourist tax (VISITAX) applies per person and is currently in the $15&ndash;20 range&mdash;paid online in advance through the official visitax.gob.mx portal (or at an airport kiosk on departure), not added to your resort bill. It's separate from any hotel charges, so budget for it independently and watch for lookalike third-party sites that mark up the fee.</li>
    <li>Review your bill before signing, all charges require a signature.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Departure</h2>
  <p>Transfer companies often schedule pickup about three hours before your flight, though 2 to 2.5 hours is usually enough, email your provider if you'd like a later pickup. On a late flight, you can check out at 11am, have the resort hold your bags, and use a spa shower so you're not rushing through your last day.</p>

  <h2>One last thing</h2>
  <p>This is easiest to enjoy when you give yourself permission to relax into it. Follow your comfort level, talk with your partner, respect other people's boundaries, and let the resort's rhythm carry you. Go in curious and open, and make it your own.</p>
